{
  "about": [
    "What the bot sends that the phone app reads (app/src/app/node/replies.ts), so changing a reply can't silently break the app.",
    "tests/test_app_replies.py runs each case against the bot's real commands and checks the messages are exactly these; the app's tests (replies.spec.ts) check it reads each as `parsed`.",
    "A case: `before`, steps run first ([sender, text]); then `as` sends `send`. `reply` is what comes back to `as`; or, with `to`, the direct messages the node sends `to` meanwhile (a notice).",
    "A `split` case: the bot splits `text` into `reply`, and the app puts it back together.",
    "Mailbox cases: Dana's passphrase in them is correcthorse12; a fixture's passphrase is never a real one.",
    "Email cases fake the node's `mail` (`email` says how it fails, if it does); weather cases give the weather the node would fetch (`weather`, or `weather_error`)."
  ],
  "senders": {
    "Admin": "ad",
    "Dana": "d0",
    "Erin": "e0",
    "BobNode": "b0",
    "Bob (base)": "bb"
  },
